0..52 Comment "// What a secret may not do, refused where it would."
53..55 Comment "//"
56..129 Comment "// A secret proves a host\'s identity, so it must stay in the process that"
130..207 Comment "// read it. A value that crossed to another world, printed, or compared would"
208..225 Comment "// leak it there."
226..228 Comment "//"
229..304 Comment "// A `Secret.T` is sealed with no mark, so the crossing judgement refuses a"
305..378 Comment "// migration\'s result holding one, and a thunk capturing one. No model of"
379..453 Comment "// equality answers at `Secret.T`, so comparing two is refused, naming it."
454..456 Comment "//"
457..524 Comment "// - see: `library/std/src/secret.gandr` — `Secret` and `Secrets`"
525..603 Comment "// - see: `immobile-crossing.gandr` — the same refusals at a seat\'s dispatch"
605..645 Comment "// The operator\'s and the seat\'s worlds."
